  "Comments": "Vapor pressure to be checked: the open sources don't give one, so the curve passes through the Joback boiling point with the Kistiakowsky heat of vaporization. Normal boiling point 569.4 K from that curve. Tc, Pc and the ideal gas formation enthalpy and Gibbs energy by Joback (1987) from that boiling point, acentric factor by Lee-Kesler. Heat of vaporization from the slope of the vapor pressure curve (50.6 kJ/mol at the boiling point), carried with Watson's exponent. Heat capacities, transport properties and surface tension of P-cymene (ChemSep), per unit mass. Liquid density 918 kg/m3 at 20 C (to be checked). UNIFAC groups approximate. Its volatility from water in a juice comes from the Henry constant of the juice package.",
